diff -ruN a/src/doc/rustc/src/platform-support/korin.md b/src/doc/rustc/src/platform-support/korin.md
--- a/src/doc/rustc/src/platform-support/korin.md
+++ b/src/doc/rustc/src/platform-support/korin.md
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# `*-unknown-korin`
+
+**Tier: 3**
+
+Korin OS: a microkernel operating system for the Raspberry Pi 4 (`aarch64-unknown-korin`) and x86-64 PCs
+(`x86_64-unknown-korin`). Its POSIX layer is newlib 4.4 with `libposix`, on which `std` takes the generic Unix paths
+(threads, files, processes with `fork` and `exec`, sockets, `dlopen`).
+
+## Target maintainers
+
+The Korin OS project.
+
+## Requirements
+
+The targets are cross-compiled from Linux, and also compiled on Korin itself. Binaries are ELF:
+
+- executables are linked without PIE at the fixed address of `libposix`'s linker script (`posix.ld`); TLS is native,
+  `thread_local!` destructors go through `pthread_key`;
+- shared objects (`cdylib`, `proc-macro`) are `dlopen` modules: PIC, their libc, allocator, threads and unwinder
+  come from the host program, which exports them (`-rdynamic`);
+- panics unwind with libgcc's unwinder, one per process, shared with the modules.
+
+The C toolchain is GCC 14 for `aarch64-onyx-elf` or `x86_64-onyx-elf` with the `posix.specs` of `libposix`. On Korin,
+that GCC is `gcc` on the `PATH` and is the default linker. When cross-compiling, set `linker` to a wrapper that adds
+the specs (`gcc -specs=.../posix.specs`).
+
+`aarch64-unknown-korin` targets the Cortex-A72 (`+v8a,+crc`, no LSE: LL/SC atomics inline). `x86_64-unknown-korin`
+targets baseline x86-64.
+
+## Building the target
+
+Add the target to `build.target` in `bootstrap.toml`, with the C toolchain of Korin:
+
+```toml
+[build]
+target = ["x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu", "x86_64-unknown-korin"]
+
+[target.x86_64-unknown-korin]
+cc = "/path/to/x86_64-korin-gcc"
+cxx = "/path/to/x86_64-korin-g++"
+ar = "/path/to/x86_64-onyx-elf-ar"
+linker = "/path/to/x86_64-korin-gcc"
+```
+
+## Building Rust programs
+
+```toml
+[target.x86_64-unknown-korin]
+linker = "/path/to/x86_64-korin-gcc"
+```
+
+then `cargo build --target x86_64-unknown-korin`.
+
+## Testing
+
+The Rust test suite is not run for these targets. `std`'s integration tests (`library/std/tests`) pass on Korin
+under QEMU (466 of 467: `env::test_self_exe_path` fails).
+
+## Cross-compilation toolchains and C code
+
+C code is compiled by the same GCC with `posix.specs`, which provides the headers of `libposix` and newlib.
